      "writtenOn": "2026-05-05T14:57:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I hadn\u0027t noticed that you had `ecmd \u003d val \u0026 0xff`, so I was thinking you were checking the entire value of the ECMD register, not just the lower 8 bits of it.\n\nI wasn\u0027t thinking about validating operand A and B values... Now thinking about it: I _hope_ we don\u0027t need to validate them, since according to VT-d spec section 10.5 \"Performance Monitoring Counter Configuration Error Checks\", an invalid Counter Number in operand A will be gracefully reported in the ECRSP register (and then BTW will be gracefully ignored by the host driver, it seems :)), rather than result in an undefined behavior?\n\nBTW similarly I _hope_ we don\u0027t need to check if the requested command is supported in DMA_ECMD_ECCAP3...",
      "parentUuid": "2ee2910d_93776d7b",
